  "evidencia": "Page: Roger Donaldson. Sentence: Roger Donaldson (born 15 November 1945) is an Australian-born New Zealand film director, producer and writer whose films include \"The World's Fastest Indian\" (2005), acclaimed 1981 relationship drama \"Smash Palace\", and a run of titles shot in the United States, including the Kevin Costner films \"No Way Out\" (1987) and \"Thirteen Days\" (2000), and the 1997 disaster film \"Dante's Peak\".\nPage: André Cayatte. Sentence: André Cayatte (3 February 1909, Carcassonne – 6 February 1989, Paris) was a French filmmaker and lawyer, who became known for his films centering on themes of crime, justice, and moral responsibility.\nPage: Chris Donaldson. Sentence: He is the son of film director Roger Donaldson.",
